[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3047441818","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108398#issuecomment-3047441818","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108398","id":3047441818,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61pEWa","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-08T05:44:05Z","updated_at":"2025-07-08T05:44:05Z","body":"If this is a bug, it should be pretty simple to fix to `TextEdit::_move_caret_left` and `TextEdit::_move_caret_right`.\nIf it's intentional, there should be an editor setting to enable symmetrical behaviour.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3047441818/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3048405792","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108398#issuecomment-3048405792","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108398","id":3048405792,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61svsg","user":{"login":"miv391","id":49998025,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTk4MDI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49998025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391","html_url":"https://github.com/miv391","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-08T10:55:41Z","updated_at":"2025-07-08T10:55:41Z","body":"vscode works quite similarly as Godot, except Godot jumps over some operators and brackets. (There are a lot of commands in vscode, so I'm sure it's easy to configure it to work differently.)\n\nIn my opinion the current commands work fine as they work with word beginnings and ends. Surely there could be new commands that work with word boundaries, whatever the word boundary definition would be.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3048405792/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3050259961","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108398#issuecomment-3050259961","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108398","id":3050259961,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61z0X5","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-08T20:47:40Z","updated_at":"2025-07-08T20:47:40Z","body":"> vscode works quite similarly as Godot, except Godot jumps over some operators and brackets. (There are a lot of commands in vscode, so I'm sure it's easy to configure it to work differently.)\n> \n> In my opinion the current commands work fine as they work with word beginnings and ends. Surely there could be new commands that work with word boundaries, whatever the word boundary definition would be.\n\nIt seems like Godot is taking a lot from VSCode, which is understandable if that is what the majority of Godot users are using.\n\nI think a big element of the pain point here is that Godot lets you specify new _word separator_ chars, not new _word constituent_ chars. Even if you disable the default separators, it still includes some mandatory defaults. As a result the user can only make this feature _less_ granular, not more, so you end up skipping over huge chunks of text, and when you want to go back, it doesn't even go to the same place you were last.\n\nIf you come from VSCode, this might be more familiar, but for people who come from VS, where the stops are super granular and symmetrical, this behaviour is very jarring. Even after years of using Godot, I still can't get around it. I really think there ought to at least be an option to allow for symmetrical stops.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3050259961/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3050280052","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108398#issuecomment-3050280052","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108398","id":3050280052,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61z5R0","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-08T20:56:51Z","updated_at":"2025-07-08T20:56:51Z","body":"I think another good reason for this being configurable is that this is more than just an editor setting - it's the behaviour of `TextEdit`, which is a runtime control. It doesn't make a lot of sense to force not only all Godot users, but Godot game players to adopt a VSCode scheme.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3050280052/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3591750829","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108398#issuecomment-3591750829","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108398","id":3591750829,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7WFcSt","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-29T15:26:35Z","updated_at":"2025-11-29T15:26:35Z","body":"Can still confirm this behavior on `v4.6.dev4`.\n\nI've checked the behavior from VSCode, and indeed it seems quite similar. But it's not something I notice too much, so I can't really have an opinion on the correct behavior. But I agree that this is very subjective and up to user preference, so it would be good to make this configurable.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3591750829/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3770905245","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108398#issuecomment-3770905245","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108398","id":3770905245,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gw3Kd","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-20T03:46:15Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T03:46:15Z","body":"Made a little workaround addon here under \"Better Caret Skips\" in the meantime:\nhttps://codeberg.org/MajorMcDoom/cozy-cube-godot-addons","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3770905245/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3775265541","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108398#issuecomment-3775265541","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108398","id":3775265541,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hBfsF","user":{"login":"kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-20T22:33:30Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T22:44:09Z","body":"I wouldn't call the current behavior asymmetrical, the caret moves the same way both left and right. It moves past all whitespace and then characters until the next whitespace. This does mean the caret doesn't go to the same position when moving left and right.\n\nThis behavior is used in VSCode, Rider, SublimeText, and Zed. \nKate and web browsers seem to always go to the start of the word like I think you are suggesting.\n\nSo the current behavior is intentional and I don't think we should change the default at least. It seems it is a matter of preference whether you want move word right to go the the end of the current word or to the start of the next one. \n\n- Also symbols being ignored is a separate issue, see https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/92981\n\nEdit: Apparently it is configurable in Rider \"Caret Movement When moving by words:\" with multiple options  https://www.jetbrains.com/help/rider/Settings_Editor_General.html","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3775265541/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3775334890","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108398#issuecomment-3775334890","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108398","id":3775334890,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hBwnq","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-20T22:55:35Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T22:55:35Z","body":"> I wouldn't call the current behavior asymmetrical, the caret moves the same way both left and right. It moves past all whitespace and then characters until the next whitespace. This does mean the caret doesn't go to the same position when moving left and right.\n\nWhat it's called isn't really relevant until this becomes a proposal or PR and there is a need for user-facing labels.\n\n> This behavior is used in VSCode, Rider, SublimeText, and Zed. Kate and web browsers seem to always go to the start of the word like I think you are suggesting.\n\nIt's not just web browsers that use skip-to-word-start. It's also Visual Studio, Notepad, Unity, LibreOffice, Steam, and more.\n\n> So the current behavior is intentional and I don't think we should change the default at least. It seems it is a matter of preference whether you want move word right to go the the end of the current word or to the start of the next one.\n\nIn the discussions, we already determined it is intentional. Configurability would be ideal.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3775334890/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]